## Rotating Card – CSS Only

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card (a `<div>` with some content) that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  The Card ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Hover Effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* rotate 180° around Y‑axis */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣  Front & Back Faces ---------- */
.card .face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;      /* hide the back side when turned */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #333;
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

.card .front {
  background: #f9f9f9;
}

.card .back {
  background: #e0e0e0;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* flip the back face so it shows correctly */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front Face -->
    <div class="face front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Hover over this card to see the rotation.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Back Face -->
    <div class="face back">
      <h2>Back Side</h2>
      <p>Here is the other side of the card.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper | Gives the 3D effect a depth cue. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` on the card | Keeps child elements (faces) in 3D space. |
| **3** | `transition` on the card | Smoothly animates the transform. |
| **4** | `:hover` changes `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| **5** | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away. |
| **6** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on the back face | Flips the back face so it appears correctly after the card rotates. |

Feel free to tweak the dimensions, colors, or the rotation axis (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) to fit your design. Happy coding!
